    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you give me a quick summary of the mandatory steps a company has to follow when a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? i need to outline the process for an internal memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When receiving a \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR, a company must first verify the user's identity to ensure the request is legitimate. Next, you must assess whether there is a legal basis or overriding legitimate interest that prevents fulfilling the request. If no such grounds exist, the company must then erase or anonymize the personal data across all systems, notifying relevant third parties if necessary. Finally, the company needs to reply to the user within one month, confirming the action taken.",
